      "writtenOn": "2023-05-17T11:10:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s true. The current upstream implementation assumes creating a new thread, it is additional ~1kB of RAM (stack, thread structures etc.). I\u0027m working on adding a new config not to create the new thread. This should allow calling the `task` function from the main thread. I think it is the only way to reclaim the main thread resources. The host command task looks like a good candidate for that",
